<pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="Ida19e75166e1282732810cf45be21e59515d88e2" commit="4cd63e9736f0cffb13eac68cb48f6eedd144ea34" commit_message="tpm2: add TPM_Clear command processing  The command is sent in session mode, but has no parameters associated with it.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:50645 TEST=with the following patches verified that TPM_Clear command is      handled successfully by the TPM.  Change-Id: Ida19e75166e1282732810cf45be21e59515d88e2 Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/357973 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="357973" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/73/357973/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="I69e5ada65a5f15a8c04be9def92a8e1f4b753d9a" commit="d03e4ccdf7bb853d3d35d2b4502c117693a86409" commit_message="tpm2: use pcr0 dependent nvram define space policy  The TPM2 specification allows defining NV ram spaces in such manner, that it is impossible to remove the space, unless a certain PCR is in a certain state.  This comes in handy when defining spaces for rollback counters: make their removal depend on PCR0 being in the default state. Then extend PCR0 to any value. This will guarantee that the spaces can not be deleted.  Also, there is no need in creating firmware and kernel rollback spaces with different privileges: they both can be created with the same set of properties, the firmware space could be locked by the RO firmware, and the kernel space could be locked by the RW firmware thus providing necessary privilege levels.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:50645, chrome-os-partner:55063 TEST=with the rest of the patches applied it is possible to boot into       Chrome OS maintaining two rollback counter spaces in the TPM NV       ram locked at different phases of the boot process.  Change-Id: I69e5ada65a5f15a8c04be9def92a8e1f4b753d9a Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/358094 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="358094" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/94/358094/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="I2a0e62527ad46f9dd060afe5e75c7e4d56752849" commit="18832e8c5d82bd42c047e030129c47a0a53d2cf8" commit_message="tpm2: implement tlcl_force_clear and use it before factory initialization  tlcl_force_clear() needs to be issued each time when the device mode switches between normal/development/recovery.  This patch adds command implementation using TPM_Clear TPM2 command, and also invokes it before factory initialization.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:50645 TEST=verified that TPM_Clear command succeeds at factory startup and      the boot proceeds normally.  Change-Id: I2a0e62527ad46f9dd060afe5e75c7e4d56752849 Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/358095 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Darren Krahn &lt;dkrahn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="358095" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/95/358095/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="I914ab6509d3ab2082152652205802201a6637fcc" commit="56416a4158b507edcddb9dd8998ae0159214c55b" commit_message="tpm2: fix tpm_write() error reporting  The code misses the cases when a response was received but the command failed. This patch fixes the problem.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:50645 TEST=none  Change-Id: I914ab6509d3ab2082152652205802201a6637fcc Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/358096 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="358096" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/96/358096/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="I62f22b9991522d4309cccc44180a5ebd4dca488d" commit="a6d4d033cd3f8724d3dbc84063d234cb81b5557b" commit_message="tpm2: implement locking firmware rollback counter  TPM1.2 is using the somewhat misnamed tlcl_set_global_lock() command function to lock the hardware rollback counter. For TPM2 let's implement and use the TPM2 command to lock an NV Ram location (TPM2_NV_WriteLock).  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:50645 TEST=verified that TPM2_NV_WriteLock command is invoked before RO      firmware starts RW, and succeeds.  Change-Id: I62f22b9991522d4309cccc44180a5ebd4dca488d Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/358097 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Darren Krahn &lt;dkrahn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="358097" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/97/358097/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="I1a9bab7396fdb652e2e3bc8529b828ea3423d851" commit="7cdb20a2c3a10566ae0b6b123f915785bac933ed" commit_message="tpm2: implement and use pcr_extend command  TPM PCRs are used in Chrome OS for two purposes: to communicate crucial information from RO firmware and to protect FW and kernel rollback counters from being deleted.  As implemented in TPM1 compatible way, the PCR extension command requires a prebuilt digest to calculate a new PCR value.  TPM2 specification introduces a PCR_Event command, where the TPM itself calculates the digest of an arbitrary length string, and then uses the calculated digest for PCR extension. PCR_Event could be a better option for Chrome OS, this needs to be investigated separately.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:50645 TEST=verified that the two PCRs are successfully extended before the      RW firmware is called.  Change-Id: I1a9bab7396fdb652e2e3bc8529b828ea3423d851 Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/358098 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Darren Krahn &lt;dkrahn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="358098" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/98/358098/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I79199a51b421c27c7122325100cdf2c980ec213d" commit="6dc41e9a170307573d977fddb3e18906949811b6" commit_message="Update all programmer init functions to register bus programmers into common list  Corresponds to r1475 from upstream. The primary change is that there are no more global variables to store each programmer type. The flashctx struct now contains a registered programmer struct, which contains a union of the three programmer structs (spi, opaque, par). When a programmer of any type is registered, it is inserted into a list called registered_programmers.  Note (from upstream): flashrom -f -c FOO -r forced_read.bin does not work anymore. We have to find an architecturally clean way to solve this.  For a full list of changes, please see the corresponding commit log from upstream.  Important: This patch is dependent on a subsequent patch which changes cros_ec to use a global variable. This dependency is indicated below.  BUG=chromium:478356 BRANCH=none TEST=reads/writes correctly to paine, but needs more testing CQ-DEPEND=CL:357911  Change-Id: I79199a51b421c27c7122325100cdf2c980ec213d Signed-off-by: Souvik Ghosh &lt;souvikghosh@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/358012 Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="358012" owner_email="souvikghosh@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="10" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/12/358012/10" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ied9b0b39b46c3377441a2550cd1479b5b081d3a9" commit="5abe959d4eef311ac7c61af9bc5d9d66e3ee5d78" commit_message="cros_ec: Create global variable for private data  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=needs testing  Change-Id: Ied9b0b39b46c3377441a2550cd1479b5b081d3a9 Signed-off-by: Souvik Ghosh &lt;souvikghosh@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/357911 Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="357911" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="13" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/11/357911/13" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4ab0885728d2bf310e76f53a5fc0ae2664583549" commit="873bbe1300ad7b70c20062b943288db40b828846" commit_message="chaps: depend on trousers even if USE=tpm is not set  Even when USE=&quot;-tpm -tpm2&quot;, chaps still depends on some header files from trousers to handle the fallback case of no TPM.  BUG=none TEST=emerging chaps pulls in trousers as a dependency  Change-Id: I4ab0885728d2bf310e76f53a5fc0ae2664583549 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/359047 Commit-Ready: Stephen Barber &lt;smbarber@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Stephen Barber &lt;smbarber@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="359047" owner_email="smbarber@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/47/359047/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="Ie18272003234ebdd218c291307c08f4aac63d4fe" commit="55bbf775527e7b75d85974b60fe3c64ba3161c1e" commit_message="FROMLIST: ath10k: fix pktlog retries offset  It is observed in pktlog dumps, failure % are not correct. Firmware sends rts/data fail count at offset 21 and 22. With Smart Antenna enabled, 21 and 22 offsets are used for tx feedback retries. Instead of overwiting the rts/data fail count, firmware sends retries at offset 31 and 32 with PKTLOG_INFO_FLAG_HW_STATUS_V2 flags. To maintain the backward compatibility, both older offset and new offset are used to read the buffers.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:35254 TEST=pktlog RTS, data failure % working with firmware 10.2.4.70.48  Change-Id: Ie18272003234ebdd218c291307c08f4aac63d4fe Signed-off-by: Anilkumar Kolli &lt;akolli@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/355414 Commit-Ready: Yixiang Li &lt;yixiang@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Yixiang Li &lt;yixiang@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Yixiang Li &lt;yixiang@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="355414" owner_email="akolli@qti.qualcomm.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/14/355414/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If33e80732a686eccf88ebd2585e00f9de6200bc5" commit="05b2dcf377954f02e301c3fba1a864c784944e75" commit_message="cryptohome: use different lockbox index for TPM2  TPM2 has a different index scheme than TPM1.2. Add the new address for TPM2, and decide between them based on the tpm2 USE flag.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54708 TEST=install_attributes succeeds on kevin  Change-Id: If33e80732a686eccf88ebd2585e00f9de6200bc5 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/357971 Commit-Ready: Stephen Barber &lt;smbarber@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Stephen Barber &lt;smbarber@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Darren Krahn &lt;dkrahn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="357971" owner_email="smbarber@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/71/357971/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.10" change_id="I1179c0ecfd484dffc9d9f519d64dff386a1a88ce" commit="0592d0870abbe3c2588835f7f0c617f2f294a9bb" commit_message="CHROMIUM: video: tegra: nvmap: fix unbalanced nvmap handle  In destroy_client we don't need to decrease the count for the nvmap handle of foreign dmabuf because that has been done in the routine nvmap_create_handle_from_fd.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:55017, chromium:478339 TEST=No more crashes caused by unbalanced nvmap handle  Change-Id: I1179c0ecfd484dffc9d9f519d64dff386a1a88ce Signed-off-by: Vince Hsu &lt;vince.h@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/358533 Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="358533" owner_email="vince.h@nvidia.com" pass_cou